{"agent":"exp13-version-cut","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`rest = old[e.end() + 1 :]` preserves everything below the region verbatim, and the freshly rendered version section is inserted *above* it. The region therefore accumulates one copy of the version section per run: on a second run for the same version (e.g. the first run committed CHANGELOG.md, then the later tag/push step failed and the cut is re-run) the temporary tag at the new branch tip renders the identical `## [x.y.z] - date` / `### Added ...` block, `rest` still contains the block committed by the first run, and the file ends up with the section twice, plus a second `[x.y.z]: ...` link line from `_relink` (which also rewrites `[Unreleased]:` again). The `if new == old: return \"unchanged\"` guard can never fire in this situation, because the duplicate copy always makes `new != old`, so `commit_on` commits the corrupted file. Note this is not fixed by `--force`; `force` only skips the hand-edit/dirty checks and the duplication is re-applied.","digest":"f8414f3bd0d08143","location":"ddflow/services/changelog_cut.py `_region` — the `new = old[: b.start()] + EW.region_text(DOC, unreleased) + \"\\n\" + new_section + rest` line","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/changelog_cut.py `_region` — the `new = old[: b.start()] + EW.region_text(DOC, unreleased) + \"\\n\" + new_section + rest` line"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":33034,"diff_sha":"27a7f9ed8ee6533c64c8d9966eee764892b4a66a239bed9c6d9966cdbd8f8c3c","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-export-version-cut","elapsed_s":1834.7,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/changelog_cut.py `_region` — the `new = old[: b.start()] + EW.region_text(DOC, unreleased) + \"\\n\" + new_section + rest` line"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e2c5fc0ff60ef9b3d6189ca60","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":10824,"schema":1,"subject":"B-export-version-cut","ts":"2026-10-02T17:28:19.704472Z"}
